{%- comment -%}
  Optical size for a residence's brochure face. Each face draws its letters
  at a different height for the same font-size (a script's capital sits
  low, Papyrus runs tall), so the same nominal size gives names of very
  different weight on the page. The figures come from the drawn height of
  each name's letters in its font file (14 Sep 2026), normalised so every
  name reads at the same height. 1 = no change.

    {% capture s %}{% render 'residence-face-scale', product: product %}{% endcapture %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign fam = product.metafields.custom.name_font.value | strip | downcase
  case fam
    when 'sephir'
      echo '1.09'
    when 'century expanded'
      echo '0.92'
    when 'hello paris serif'
      echo '1.14'
    when 'adu script'
      echo '1.55'
    when 'papyrus'
      echo '0.68'
    when 'garamond'
      echo '1.05'
    else
      echo '1'
  endcase
-%}
